{
  "comment": "The sounds tools/fetch_audio.py fetches: files and archives (zip, 7z, rar) at fixed URLs or itch.io uploads; the files picked from under `root` by pattern are prepared by their kind (targets: loudness in LUFS, true-peak ceiling in dBTP, channels, format, Vorbis quality) and written to <dest>, cc0/ or ccby/ by licence. sfx: trimmed mono WAV; loop, music, jingle: stereo Ogg; mono: an Ogg as mono WAV (Kenney's placeholders); keep: as it is. Optional per item: cut [start, end] s, split (takes cut at silences), seam s (a loop's crossfade), gain dB, rename; each a value or a map by file. mixes: ambience beds made of layers (sources by id). credit: what CREDITS.md says. audio.lock.json records each download's sha256.",
  "roots": ["cc0", "ccby"],
  "targets": {
    "sfx": {"lufs": -18, "ceiling": -1, "channels": 1, "format": "wav"},
